    {
      "id": "E22",
      "chapter": 22,
      "slug": "22-continuous-time-chains",
      "section": "22.9",
      "lang": "en",
      "title": "Same jump chain, different lifetimes",
      "html": "<figure class=\"batch3\" id=\"visual-E22\" data-batch3=\"E22\" lang=\"en\"><header><span>E22</span><h3>Same jump chain, different lifetimes</h3></header><p>The state sequence is identical. Only the holding laws change. The lengths below are expectations, not a time bound on a sample path.</p><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-clock-n=\"4\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Expand first 4 states</button><button type=\"button\" data-clock-n=\"6\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Expand first 6 states</button></div><div class=\"b3-pair\"><section><h4>Constant rates: no finite endpoint</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/E22-en-4-0.svg\" alt=\"Equal mean holding times continue without a finite endpoint\" data-constant></section><section><h4>Doubling rates: means sum to one</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/E22-en-4-1.svg\" alt=\"Geometric mean waits with an explicitly marked remaining tail\" data-fast></section></div><figcaption id=\"visual-E22-end\">Exact model: a pure-birth chain j→j+1 started at 1, with independent unit exponentials Ej, waits τj=Ej/λj and lifetime ζ=Στj. For λj=1, the iid strong law gives ζ=∞ almost surely; infinite expectation alone would not prove this. For λj=2^j, Tonelli gives Eζ=Σ2^(-j)=1, hence ζ<∞ almost surely by nonnegativity. Each wait is strictly positive and each rate finite. The unfilled tail has mean 2^(-n); this asserts neither ζ≤1 nor that displayed mean lengths are sample waits. The two diagrams use different display units, not a shared calendar axis. No post-explosion restart is constructed.</figcaption><nav><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/E22.en.svg\">SVG</a><a href=\"/print/E22.en.html\">Static print</a></nav></figure>",
      "condition": "Exact model: a pure-birth chain j→j+1 started at 1, with independent unit exponentials Ej, waits τj=Ej/λj and lifetime ζ=Στj. For λj=1, the iid strong law gives ζ=∞ almost surely; infinite expectation alone would not prove this. For λj=2^j, Tonelli gives Eζ=Σ2^(-j)=1, hence ζ<∞ almost surely by nonnegativity. Each wait is strictly positive and each rate finite. The unfilled tail has mean 2^(-n); this asserts neither ζ≤1 nor that displayed mean lengths are sample waits. The two diagrams use different display units, not a shared calendar axis. No post-explosion restart is constructed.",
      "status": "author visual review pending",
      "kind": "new explanatory figure",
      "asset_base": "/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/"
    },
    {
      "id": "E28",
      "chapter": 28,
      "slug": "28-semigroups",
      "section": "28.1",
      "lang": "zh",
      "title": "同一个核，两个方向的平均",
      "html": "<figure class=\"batch3\" id=\"visual-E28\" data-batch3=\"E28\" lang=\"zh\"><header><span>E28</span><h3>同一个核，两个方向的平均</h3></header><p>左边把出发质量送到未来；右边把未来收益拉回每个出发点。箭头方向不同，转移概率始终是同一个P。</p><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-mu=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"false\">μ(A)=0.0</button><button type=\"button\" data-mu=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"false\">μ(A)=0.5</button><button type=\"button\" data-mu=\"2\" aria-pressed=\"true\">μ(A)=1.0</button></div><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-payoff=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"true\">f(A)=0, f(B)=4</button><button type=\"button\" data-payoff=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"false\">f(A)=4, f(B)=0</button></div><div class=\"b3-pair\"><section><h4>推动分布</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/E28-zh-2-0-0.svg\" alt=\"Starting and final probability strips, forward arrows\" data-push></section><section><h4>拉回收益</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/E28-zh-2-0-1.svg\" alt=\"Future payoffs and conditional expected payoffs, backward arrows\" data-pull></section></div><output data-pairing>两边得到同一总平均：(μP)f = μ(Tf) = 1</output><figcaption id=\"visual-E28-end\">有限状态精确核：行是出发状态、列是到达状态，对角3/4、非对角1/4。左下色条长度表示质量，右图数值是收益，不是概率；所有箭头只是运算方向，不以线宽编码流量。Tf=(3f(A)/4+f(B)/4, f(A)/4+3f(B)/4)。独立选择μ与f，有限求和交换给Σᵧ(ΣₓμₓPₓᵧ)fᵧ=Σₓμₓ(ΣᵧPₓᵧfᵧ)。本图只解释一个固定时刻的核及其对偶作用，不以单个矩阵证明连续时间半群、生成元或Feller条件。</figcaption><nav><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/E28.zh.svg\">SVG</a><a href=\"/print/E28.zh.html\">静态打印</a></nav></figure>",
      "condition": "有限状态精确核：行是出发状态、列是到达状态，对角3/4、非对角1/4。左下色条长度表示质量，右图数值是收益，不是概率；所有箭头只是运算方向，不以线宽编码流量。Tf=(3f(A)/4+f(B)/4, f(A)/4+3f(B)/4)。独立选择μ与f，有限求和交换给Σᵧ(ΣₓμₓPₓᵧ)fᵧ=Σₓμₓ(ΣᵧPₓᵧfᵧ)。本图只解释一个固定时刻的核及其对偶作用，不以单个矩阵证明连续时间半群、生成元或Feller条件。",
      "status": "author visual review pending",
      "kind": "new explanatory figure",
      "asset_base": "/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/"
    },
    {
      "id": "E28",
      "chapter": 28,
      "slug": "28-semigroups",
      "section": "28.1",
      "lang": "en",
      "title": "One kernel, two directions of averaging",
      "html": "<figure class=\"batch3\" id=\"visual-E28\" data-batch3=\"E28\" lang=\"en\"><header><span>E28</span><h3>One kernel, two directions of averaging</h3></header><p>The left view pushes starting mass into the future. The right view pulls future payoffs back to each starting point. The directions differ; the transition probabilities are the same P.</p><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-mu=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"false\">μ(A)=0.0</button><button type=\"button\" data-mu=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"false\">μ(A)=0.5</button><button type=\"button\" data-mu=\"2\" aria-pressed=\"true\">μ(A)=1.0</button></div><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-payoff=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"true\">f(A)=0, f(B)=4</button><button type=\"button\" data-payoff=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"false\">f(A)=4, f(B)=0</button></div><div class=\"b3-pair\"><section><h4>Push the distribution</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/E28-en-2-0-0.svg\" alt=\"Starting and final probability strips, forward arrows\" data-push></section><section><h4>Pull back the payoff</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/E28-en-2-0-1.svg\" alt=\"Future payoffs and conditional expected payoffs, backward arrows\" data-pull></section></div><output data-pairing>Both give the same total mean: (μP)f = μ(Tf) = 1</output><figcaption id=\"visual-E28-end\">Exact two-state kernel: rows are departure states, columns arrival states, diagonal 3/4 and off-diagonal 1/4. Strip lengths encode probabilities; the right-hand numbers are payoffs, not probabilities. Arrows indicate operation direction, never flow magnitude. Tf=(3f(A)/4+f(B)/4, f(A)/4+3f(B)/4). For independently selected μ and f, interchanging finite sums gives Σy(Σx μx Pxy)fy=Σx μx(Σy Pxy fy). One fixed-time kernel illustrates dual actions; it does not establish a continuous-time semigroup, a generator or the Feller property.</figcaption><nav><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/E28.en.svg\">SVG</a><a href=\"/print/E28.en.html\">Static print</a></nav></figure>",
      "condition": "Exact two-state kernel: rows are departure states, columns arrival states, diagonal 3/4 and off-diagonal 1/4. Strip lengths encode probabilities; the right-hand numbers are payoffs, not probabilities. Arrows indicate operation direction, never flow magnitude. Tf=(3f(A)/4+f(B)/4, f(A)/4+3f(B)/4). For independently selected μ and f, interchanging finite sums gives Σy(Σx μx Pxy)fy=Σx μx(Σy Pxy fy). One fixed-time kernel illustrates dual actions; it does not establish a continuous-time semigroup, a generator or the Feller property.",
      "status": "author visual review pending",
      "kind": "new explanatory figure",
      "asset_base": "/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/"
    },
    {
      "id": "E39",
      "chapter": 39,
      "slug": "39-malliavin",
      "section": "39.14",
      "lang": "zh",
      "title": "两个坐标，不一定有两个方向",
      "html": "<figure class=\"batch3\" id=\"visual-E39\" data-batch3=\"E39\" lang=\"zh\"><header><span>E39</span><h3>两个坐标，不一定有两个方向</h3></header><p>轻推同一路径中的两个正交噪声读数，检查输出能否独立移动。这是噪声方向的微分，不是路径的时间导数。</p><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-noise=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"true\">看两个方向</button><button type=\"button\" data-noise=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"false\">只推动Z₂</button></div><div class=\"b3-pair\"><section><h4>重复信息：秩1</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/E39-zh-0-0.svg\" alt=\"A noise perturbation square maps to a line\" data-rank-one></section><section><h4>不同响应：秩2</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/E39-zh-1-0.svg\" alt=\"The same perturbation square maps to a parallelogram\" data-rank-two></section></div><div class=\"b3-mobile\"><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/E39-zh-compact-0.svg\" alt=\"Both rank structures in a dedicated compact layout\" data-rank-compact></div><output>左 det γ = 0；右 det γ = 1。差别来自响应方向，不是Brownian路径的条数。</output><figcaption id=\"visual-E39-end\">取同一Brownian运动上Z₁=B₁、Z₂=√12(∫₀¹Bₛds−B₁/2)=∫₀¹√12(1/2−s)dBₛ。两个核在L²[0,1]中正交且范数1，故(Z₁,Z₂)为独立标准正态。左响应矩阵[[1,0],[2,0]]，γ=[[1,2],[2,4]]；右[[1,0],[1,1]]，γ=[[1,1],[1,2]]。图画[-1,1]²噪声扰动方块的线性像，不是密度热图，也不把方块当作Gaussian支撑。这里的线性Gaussian例子右侧有光滑密度，不能据此宣称任意可Malliavin微分输出都有光滑密度；一般结论还需正文的非退化与可积性条件。</figcaption><nav><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/E39.zh.svg\">SVG</a><a href=\"/print/E39.zh.html\">静态打印</a></nav></figure>",
      "condition": "取同一Brownian运动上Z₁=B₁、Z₂=√12(∫₀¹Bₛds−B₁/2)=∫₀¹√12(1/2−s)dBₛ。两个核在L²[0,1]中正交且范数1，故(Z₁,Z₂)为独立标准正态。左响应矩阵[[1,0],[2,0]]，γ=[[1,2],[2,4]]；右[[1,0],[1,1]]，γ=[[1,1],[1,2]]。图画[-1,1]²噪声扰动方块的线性像，不是密度热图，也不把方块当作Gaussian支撑。这里的线性Gaussian例子右侧有光滑密度，不能据此宣称任意可Malliavin微分输出都有光滑密度；一般结论还需正文的非退化与可积性条件。",
      "status": "author visual review pending",
      "kind": "new explanatory figure",
      "asset_base": "/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/"
    },
    {
      "id": "E39",
      "chapter": 39,
      "slug": "39-malliavin",
      "section": "39.14",
      "lang": "en",
      "title": "Two coordinates need not give two directions",
      "html": "<figure class=\"batch3\" id=\"visual-E39\" data-batch3=\"E39\" lang=\"en\"><header><span>E39</span><h3>Two coordinates need not give two directions</h3></header><p>Perturb two orthogonal readings of one path. Can the outputs move independently? These are noise directions, not time derivatives.</p><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-noise=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Show both directions</button><button type=\"button\" data-noise=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Perturb Z₂ only</button></div><div class=\"b3-pair\"><section><h4>Repeated information: rank one</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/E39-en-0-0.svg\" alt=\"A noise perturbation square maps to a line\" data-rank-one></section><section><h4>Independent responses: rank two</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/E39-en-1-0.svg\" alt=\"The same perturbation square maps to a parallelogram\" data-rank-two></section></div><div class=\"b3-mobile\"><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/E39-en-compact-0.svg\" alt=\"Both rank structures in a dedicated compact layout\" data-rank-compact></div><output>Left det γ = 0; right det γ = 1. The difference is in response directions, not the number of Brownian paths.</output><figcaption id=\"visual-E39-end\">On one Brownian path set Z1=B1 and Z2=√12(∫0^1 Bs ds−B1/2)=∫0^1 √12(1/2−s)dBs. Their L²[0,1] kernels are orthogonal unit vectors, hence Z1,Z2 are independent standard normals. Left response matrix [[1,0],[2,0]] gives γ=[[1,2],[2,4]]; right [[1,0],[1,1]] gives γ=[[1,1],[1,2]]. The drawings are linear images of the noise perturbation square [-1,1]^2, not density heat maps or bounded Gaussian supports. The full-rank linear Gaussian example has a smooth density; arbitrary Malliavin differentiability does not imply this. General results require the nondegeneracy and integrability conditions established in the text.</figcaption><nav><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/E39.en.svg\">SVG</a><a href=\"/print/E39.en.html\">Static print</a></nav></figure>",
      "condition": "On one Brownian path set Z1=B1 and Z2=√12(∫0^1 Bs ds−B1/2)=∫0^1 √12(1/2−s)dBs. Their L²[0,1] kernels are orthogonal unit vectors, hence Z1,Z2 are independent standard normals. Left response matrix [[1,0],[2,0]] gives γ=[[1,2],[2,4]]; right [[1,0],[1,1]] gives γ=[[1,1],[1,2]]. The drawings are linear images of the noise perturbation square [-1,1]^2, not density heat maps or bounded Gaussian supports. The full-rank linear Gaussian example has a smooth density; arbitrary Malliavin differentiability does not imply this. General results require the nondegeneracy and integrability conditions established in the text.",
      "status": "author visual review pending",
      "kind": "new explanatory figure",
      "asset_base": "/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v3/"
    },
    {
      "id": "E14",
      "chapter": 14,
      "slug": "14-arrays-and-stability",
      "section": "14.3",
      "title": "方差分散了，大跳仍可能留下",
      "lang": "zh",
      "html": "<figure class=\"batch2\" id=\"visual-E14\" data-batch2=\"E14\" lang=\"zh\"><header><span>E14</span><h3>方差分散了，大跳仍可能留下</h3></header><p class=\"\">两行总方差都为1，每项方差都为1/n。可是一行把方差留在±1，另一行把取值缩进了0附近。</p><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-array-n=\"4\" aria-pressed=\"false\">n=4</button><button type=\"button\" data-array-n=\"16\" aria-pressed=\"true\">n=16</button><button type=\"button\" data-array-n=\"64\" aria-pressed=\"false\">n=64</button></div><div class=\"b2-pair\"><section class=\"b2-panel\"><h4>稀少，但大小不缩</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E14-zh-16-rare.svg\" alt=\"Rare atoms stay at minus and plus one\" data-rare-scene><p class=\"b2-result\" >阈值外二阶贡献：1</p></section><section class=\"b2-panel\"><h4>每一项真正变小</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E14-zh-16-small.svg\" alt=\"Fair small increments move toward zero\" data-small-scene><p class=\"b2-result\" >阈值外二阶贡献：0</p></section></div><p class=\"b2-note\">淡带：|x|≤1/2。切换n，观察原子的位置和面积分别怎样变化。</p><figcaption id=\"visual-E14-end\">每行内部独立。左：P(Xₙₖ=±1)=1/(2n)，P(0)=1−1/n。右：P(Yₙₖ=±1/√n)=1/2。两者均中心化、总方差1，Feller最大方差1/n→0；固定ε=1/2，所有所示n≥4时Lindeberg量分别1与0（使用严格>）。左整行有至少一笔非零的概率1−(1−1/n)ⁿ→1−e⁻¹，但非零项可能互相抵消；不把这个概率等同于总和非零。左总和趋于带±1标记、强度1的复合Poisson，右趋于标准Gaussian。圆面积表示概率，横位置表示取值；方框只列第1、第2与第n项，中间项由省略号表示；一行恰有n项。阴影只标阈值，不是概率密度。</figcaption><nav><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E14.zh.svg\">SVG</a><a href=\"/print/E14.zh.html\">静态打印</a></nav></figure>",
      "condition": "每行内部独立。左：P(Xₙₖ=±1)=1/(2n)，P(0)=1−1/n。右：P(Yₙₖ=±1/√n)=1/2。两者均中心化、总方差1，Feller最大方差1/n→0；固定ε=1/2，所有所示n≥4时Lindeberg量分别1与0（使用严格>）。左整行有至少一笔非零的概率1−(1−1/n)ⁿ→1−e⁻¹，但非零项可能互相抵消；不把这个概率等同于总和非零。左总和趋于带±1标记、强度1的复合Poisson，右趋于标准Gaussian。圆面积表示概率，横位置表示取值；方框只列第1、第2与第n项，中间项由省略号表示；一行恰有n项。阴影只标阈值，不是概率密度。",
      "status": "adopted working visual; local clarification pending author check",
      "kind": "minimal author-requested clarification",
      "asset_base": "/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/"
