      "lang": "en",
      "html": "<figure class=\"batch2\" id=\"visual-E30\" data-batch2=\"E30\" lang=\"en\"><header><span>E30</span><h3>Same value at arrivals, different time rules</h3></header><p class=\"\">Both rules take value 1 at arrivals. But choosing 1 in advance and selecting only observed jump instants have different time costs.</p><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-arrival-count=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Record: 0 arrivals</button><button type=\"button\" data-arrival-count=\"2\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Record: 2 arrivals</button><button type=\"button\" data-arrival-count=\"3\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Record: 3 arrivals</button></div><div class=\"b2-pair\"><section class=\"b2-panel\"><h4>Before: choose 1 throughout</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E30-en-pre-2.svg\" alt=\"A predictable constant choice fills the whole time band\" data-pre-scene><p class=\"b2-result\" >Population expectation: 0</p></section><section class=\"b2-panel\"><h4>After: select observed jump instants</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E30-en-after-2.svg\" alt=\"Jump-only choices are isolated instants of zero time length\" data-after-scene><p class=\"b2-result\" >Population expectation: 3</p></section></div><output data-reading>Compensated payoff on this record: before 2−3=−1; after 2−0=2.</output><p class=\"\">The right-hand payoff is a pathwise Stieltjes calculation selected after jumps occur, not a legitimate predictable strategy chosen beforehand. The predictable martingale integral’s fairness does not apply.</p><figcaption id=\"visual-E30-end\">Rate-one Poisson process with its usual augmented natural filtration and K=3. The predictable choice H≡1 on (0,3] gives pathwise payoff N3−3, of expectation 0. Ht=ΔNt is adapted and optional but not predictable, so it is not a legitimate strategy chosen beforehand. Only its pathwise Stieltjes payoff is computed here, not a predictable stochastic integral; it gives N3−0, of expectation 3. Dots denote zero-duration instants, not narrow positive-length intervals. Finitely many jumps have zero dt mass but unit dN mass each. The three hand-chosen records illustrate pathwise calculations only; they are not equiprobable or simulated estimates of expectations. Expectations use E N3=3. The natural filtration and simple Poisson jumps matter; no assertion for every filtration is made.</figcaption><nav><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E30.en.svg\">SVG</a><a href=\"/print/E30.en.html\">Static print</a></nav></figure>",
      "condition": "Rate-one Poisson process with its usual augmented natural filtration and K=3. The predictable choice H≡1 on (0,3] gives pathwise payoff N3−3, of expectation 0. Ht=ΔNt is adapted and optional but not predictable, so it is not a legitimate strategy chosen beforehand. Only its pathwise Stieltjes payoff is computed here, not a predictable stochastic integral; it gives N3−0, of expectation 3. Dots denote zero-duration instants, not narrow positive-length intervals. Finitely many jumps have zero dt mass but unit dN mass each. The three hand-chosen records illustrate pathwise calculations only; they are not equiprobable or simulated estimates of expectations. Expectations use E N3=3. The natural filtration and simple Poisson jumps matter; no assertion for every filtration is made.",
